---INSTRUCTION---
Write an Elixir function `count_valid_brackets/1` that takes a string and returns the number of valid pairs of brackets in the string.

The string may contain the following bracket characters: parentheses `()`, square brackets `[]`, and curly braces `{}`. A valid pair is defined as a matching open and close bracket of the same type that are correctly nested.

The function should return an integer count of such valid pairs.

The solution should have linear time complexity, O(n), where n is the length of the string.

Edge cases:
- Empty string returns 0.
- Unmatched closing brackets are ignored (they do not form a valid pair).
- The string may contain non-bracket characters, which are to be ignored.

Example: "({})[]" returns 3.
